n_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:ba34c70f2d27d6bd0c6ef5531984d52391f2c125fcae989bbaccbaff0fc895bc","file":"preprints/Two-step-monodromy-of-special-quasi-projective-varieties-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":95,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"afa669d22998e30d855317293f559196f7336659a463de66cc8fd30f47c9d578","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Two-step-monodromy-of-special-quasi-projective-varieties-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:ba34c70f2d27d6bd0c6ef5531984d52391f2c125fcae989bbaccbaff0fc895bc","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Two-step-monodromy-of-special-quasi-projective-varieties-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L95"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:completion}\nLet $V$ be a connected smooth complex quasi-projective variety and let\n$a:V\\to A=\\Alb(V)$ be its algebraic quasi-Albanese map. Suppose $a$ is\ndominant, choose a smooth connected general fibre $F$ and a point\n$v\\in F$, and assume that the sequence of ordinary fundamental groups\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:exact}\n \\pi_1(F,v)\\longrightarrow\\Gamma:=\\pi_1(V,v)\n \\xrightarrow{a_*}\\Lambda:=\\pi_1(A,a(v))\\longrightarrow1\n\\end{equation}\nis exact. Then every canonical rational unipotent quotient of $\\Gamma$\nhas nilpotency class at most two. The full rational unipotent completion\nis a finite-dimensional unipotent algebraic group of class at most two.\nEvery finite-dimensional complex unipotent representation of $\\Gamma$\nalso has image of class at most two."}
